1
00:00:29,958 --> 00:00:30,625
Tear a piece off.

2
00:00:30,916 --> 00:00:31,750
Tear a piece off. Tear a piece off.

3
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:32,750
Alright.

4
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:34,041
Give it to me, give it to me.

5
00:00:34,041 --> 00:00:35,041
You eat.

6
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:36,250
Here.

7
00:00:37,416 --> 00:00:38,416
You eat.

8
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:49,666
Here, man.

9
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:51,083
You eat. I'm not hungry.

10
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:53,375
Uh...

11
00:00:54,083 --> 00:00:55,083
This... this...

12
00:00:55,125 --> 00:00:56,541
That's... that's too kind of you.

13
00:00:57,958 --> 00:00:58,958
It's all ours.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,333
We'll save it for tomorrow.

15
00:01:34,541 --> 00:01:35,541
Is the fuel line fixed?

16
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:40,375
No.

17
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:41,750
I'm tired. Going to sleep.

18
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,250
Lin Zai.

19
00:02:13,625 --> 00:02:14,625
Lin Zai.

20
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:24,250
Lin Zai.

21
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:36,750
Lin Zai.

22
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:12,300
"The Last Oath"

23
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:17,300
(Episode 8: Infected
Classification System)

24
00:04:33,583 --> 00:04:34,875
I'll go find some more diesel.

25
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
This sleeve...

26
00:05:29,708 --> 00:05:30,916
How did it get torn?

27
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,749
I probably snagged it
on something by accident.

28
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:34,750
It's fine.

29
00:05:35,166 --> 00:05:36,416
How can it be fine?

30
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:36,916
Here.

31
00:05:37,041 --> 00:05:38,361
Let Grandma stitch it up for you.

32
00:05:38,416 --> 00:05:39,583
It's fine, Grandma. Really.

33
00:05:40,083 --> 00:05:41,083
It'll just take a second.

34
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:43,166
Oh, you kid.

35
00:05:44,875 --> 00:05:46,041
If your family were around,

36
00:05:46,583 --> 00:05:48,000
seeing you in these torn clothes,

37
00:05:48,083 --> 00:05:49,083
running around out there,

38
00:05:49,291 --> 00:05:50,041
their hearts...

39
00:05:50,042 --> 00:05:51,250
would ache so much.

40
00:05:52,458 --> 00:05:54,000
If I were your mother,

41
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:55,750
just thinking about you out there,

42
00:05:56,208 --> 00:05:58,333
hungry and cold,

43
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:00,791
with no one to look after you,

44
00:06:01,166 --> 00:06:02,166
my heart...

45
00:06:02,916 --> 00:06:04,756
would feel like it's
being pierced by needles.

46
00:06:06,708 --> 00:06:07,708
In this day and age,

47
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:10,458
nothing is more important

48
00:06:10,625 --> 00:06:11,666
than staying safe.

49
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:14,642
You need to take good care of yourself.

50
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:15,666
You hear me?

51
00:06:21,958 --> 00:06:22,958
Look.

52
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:24,333
All stitched up.

53
00:06:31,208 --> 00:06:32,208
Is the boat fixed?

54
00:06:34,291 --> 00:06:35,208
Is that all you care about now?

55
00:06:35,209 --> 00:06:36,529
Whether the boat is fixed or not?

56
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,713
We need to get out of
here as soon as possible.

57
00:06:42,291 --> 00:06:43,331
Leave as soon as possible.

58
00:06:45,291 --> 00:06:46,291
And then what?

59
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:49,291
Is there anything else on your mind
right now besides your damn mission?

60
00:06:49,291 --> 00:06:50,291
Yes.

61
00:06:58,375 --> 00:07:00,015
Reaching headquarters as soon as possible

62
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:01,250
is best for everyone.

63
00:07:06,375 --> 00:07:07,375
Everyone.

64
00:07:08,916 --> 00:07:09,916
So you still just see me as

65
00:07:09,917 --> 00:07:10,958
an immune subject, right?

66
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,166
If I weren't immune,

67
00:07:14,291 --> 00:07:16,211
you wouldn't care if I
lived or died, would you?

68
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,250
I...

69
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,500
Fine.

70
00:07:23,875 --> 00:07:24,875
Very well.

71
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:26,583
I get it.

72
00:08:17,583 --> 00:08:18,583
It just needs some gas.

73
00:08:43,125 --> 00:08:44,125
Grandma.

74
00:08:45,916 --> 00:08:46,708
Do you know

75
00:08:46,791 --> 00:08:48,166
where the nearest town is?

76
00:08:50,083 --> 00:08:51,958
There's one five kilometers east.

77
00:08:53,416 --> 00:08:54,416
Why?

78
00:08:57,333 --> 00:08:58,583
Are you feeling unwell?

79
00:08:59,291 --> 00:09:00,291
No.

80
00:09:00,416 --> 00:09:01,750
Isn't your son injured?

81
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:03,124
I was thinking if we run out of medicine,

82
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,125
where we could restock.

83
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:07,666
You have such a good heart.

84
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Young man.

85
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,291
Young man, what's wrong?

86
00:10:00,708 --> 00:10:01,708
Young man!

87
00:10:01,958 --> 00:10:03,083
Help! Somebody!

88
00:10:03,916 --> 00:10:05,236
What's wrong with you, young man?

89
00:10:11,708 --> 00:10:12,458
What happened to him?

90
00:10:12,625 --> 00:10:13,625
I...

91
00:10:14,541 --> 00:10:16,040
He just ate some of that...

92
00:10:16,041 --> 00:10:17,791
I mashed some wild herbs and berries

93
00:10:17,875 --> 00:10:18,875
into a paste.

94
00:10:21,041 --> 00:10:22,458
He's allergic to it.

95
00:10:23,375 --> 00:10:23,625
This...

96
00:10:23,875 --> 00:10:24,958
How is that possible?

97
00:10:43,791 --> 00:10:44,791
Where's the medicine?

98
00:10:47,125 --> 00:10:49,708
I wouldn't dare touch your things!

99
00:10:51,666 --> 00:10:52,208
Oh, right.

100
00:10:52,666 --> 00:10:54,375
There should be medicine in town.

101
00:10:54,541 --> 00:10:55,791
Five kilometers east.

102
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:05,499
You should leave him here.

103
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:07,291
We'll help look after him.

104
00:11:08,291 --> 00:11:09,958
There are zombies in town.

105
00:11:11,041 --> 00:11:12,500
It won't be easy carrying him.

106
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:14,070
We'll keep an eye on him for you.

107
00:11:14,208 --> 00:11:15,333
Go and come back quickly.

108
00:11:31,875 --> 00:11:32,875
Watch him closely.

109
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:35,373
Give him plenty of water
and keep his airway clear.

110
00:11:36,916 --> 00:11:38,041
When I get back,

111
00:11:39,291 --> 00:11:41,208
if he's missing a single hair...

112
00:11:42,083 --> 00:11:43,208
Don't... don't worry.

113
00:11:43,375 --> 00:11:45,666
We'll definitely take good care of him.

114
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,208
Hurry back!

115
00:12:10,166 --> 00:12:12,416
Talk about a stroke of luck.

116
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:13,833
Go get ready.

117
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:15,583
When that kid comes back,

118
00:12:15,666 --> 00:12:16,958
we'll catch him off guard.

119
00:12:17,375 --> 00:12:17,875
Mom.

120
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:18,833
Go back inside.

121
00:12:19,041 --> 00:12:20,208
Keep a close eye on that one.

122
00:12:20,291 --> 00:12:21,411
Don't let anything go wrong.

123
00:12:21,458 --> 00:12:22,458
I know.

124
00:12:22,666 --> 00:12:23,666
Let's go.

125
00:12:34,208 --> 00:12:35,208
You...

126
00:12:35,458 --> 00:12:36,541
You're okay.

127
00:12:38,041 --> 00:12:39,458
Thanks. I'm leaving now.

128
00:12:39,708 --> 00:12:40,500
You can't do that!

129
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,125
That young man

130
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:42,416
told us to watch you.

131
00:12:43,041 --> 00:12:44,707
I'm really fine. I'm leaving.

132
00:12:44,708 --> 00:12:45,500
If you leave,

133
00:12:45,501 --> 00:12:46,517
what are we supposed to do?

134
00:12:46,541 --> 00:12:47,458
When that young man comes back

135
00:12:47,458 --> 00:12:48,041
and doesn't see you,

136
00:12:48,042 --> 00:12:49,124
he'll kill us!

137
00:12:49,125 --> 00:12:50,708
He doesn't kill innocent people.

138
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,208
Quick! Stop him!

139
00:14:15,666 --> 00:14:16,666
Meat.

140
00:14:18,208 --> 00:14:19,208
Eat meat.

141
00:14:24,291 --> 00:14:26,166
Oh, my poor child.

142
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:29,166
Mom is useless.

143
00:14:30,291 --> 00:14:31,333
Since you were little,

144
00:14:31,541 --> 00:14:33,958
I could barely give you any meat to eat.

145
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,666
Mom is so sorry.

146
00:14:39,125 --> 00:14:39,916
Mom.

147
00:14:40,125 --> 00:14:41,791
Stop saying that.

148
00:14:42,166 --> 00:14:44,208
Didn't a tender one just show up?

149
00:14:45,041 --> 00:14:46,833
How should we cook it this time?

150
00:14:59,375 --> 00:15:00,458
For Chengcai,

151
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:01,750
get a thigh.

152
00:15:02,750 --> 00:15:03,750
The ribs,

153
00:15:03,875 --> 00:15:04,875
chop them off

154
00:15:05,041 --> 00:15:06,125
and make a rib soup.

155
00:15:07,041 --> 00:15:08,208
As for the rest,

156
00:15:08,541 --> 00:15:09,666
salt and cure it.

157
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,666
It'll last us a while.

158
00:15:14,625 --> 00:15:15,625
Chengcai.

159
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,500
It's about time.

160
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:18,941
You should go ambush the other one.

161
00:15:21,958 --> 00:15:22,958
Be careful.

162
00:15:23,625 --> 00:15:24,666
He's a tough nut to crack.

163
00:15:29,625 --> 00:15:30,625
Meat.

164
00:15:31,083 --> 00:15:32,083
Meat.

165
00:15:32,333 --> 00:15:32,791
Meat.

166
00:15:32,916 --> 00:15:33,916
Be careful!

167
00:15:36,291 --> 00:15:37,291
Chengren.

168
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,083
Go get that kid

169
00:15:39,625 --> 00:15:40,625
and drag him over here.

170
00:17:30,166 --> 00:17:31,458
Let me go!

171
00:17:33,416 --> 00:17:34,416
Son!

172
00:17:35,083 --> 00:17:36,083
Son!

173
00:17:36,166 --> 00:17:37,041
Son!

174
00:17:37,041 --> 00:17:38,041
Let go of my son!

175
00:17:38,042 --> 00:17:39,250
Let go of my son!

176
00:17:39,333 --> 00:17:42,083
Let go of my son! Let go of my son!

177
00:17:51,166 --> 00:17:52,541
No one hurts my son!

178
00:18:00,375 --> 00:18:01,375
Mom!

179
00:18:02,541 --> 00:18:03,541
Mom!

180
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,166
Mom!

181
00:18:07,541 --> 00:18:08,541
Mom!

182
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:09,875
Mom!

183
00:18:10,375 --> 00:18:11,749
Mom!

184
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:12,958
Mom!

185
00:18:13,708 --> 00:18:14,791
Mom!

186
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:17,458
Mom!

187
00:18:53,416 --> 00:18:54,416
Don't!

188
00:18:54,458 --> 00:18:55,458
Don't kill me!

189
00:18:55,541 --> 00:18:56,541
I'm human!

190
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:15,750
Lin Zai!
